oquo:NominalToOrdinalScalePointMapping
        a                owl:Class ;
        rdfs:comment     "Represents the mapping of a category of a nominal scale onto a category of an ordinal scale." ;
        rdfs:label       "nominal to ordinal scale point mapping" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  oquo:ScalePointMapping ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  [ a                         owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:onClass               om-1:Measurement_scale_category ;
                           owl:onProperty            oquo:hasInputScaleCategory ;
                           owl:qualifiedCardinality  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                         ] ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  [ a                         owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:onClass               qm:OrdinalScaleItem ;
                           owl:onProperty            oquo:hasOutputScaleCategory ;
                           owl:qualifiedCardinality  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                         ] ;
        obo:IAO_0000112  "A metric that reports the serialisation format of an ontology on a nominal scale (e.g. RDF/XML, Turtle, OBO, proprietary) can be converted into a five categories ordinal scale with mappings such as RDF/XML onto category 5, Turtle onto category 5, OBO onto category 3 and proprietary onto category 1." ;
        obo:IAO_0000115  "A scale point mapping that converts a category of an input nominal scale into a category of an output ordinal scale. Each mapping has exactly one input scale category (hasInputScaleCategory) and one output ordinal scale category (hasOutputScaleCategory). A nominal to ordinal scale conversion contains one of these mappings for each category of the input scale, and several input categories may be converted into the same output category. Since the categories of a nominal scale are not ordered, the output categories express the judgement of the quality model on how each input category contributes to quality." .

